<title>UK: EBRD adds 40 bln lire to 10-year structured bond.</title>
<headline>EBRD adds 40 bln lire to 10-year structured bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Bank for Reconstruction and Development has added 40 billion lire to a 10-year structured bond, joint lead managers Banca di Roma and Morgan Stanley said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The new paper was reoffered at 96.375.</p>
<p>The total size is now 265 billion lire.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT   **40 BLN LIRE  COUPON    *10.00     MATURITY   *27.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  98.00     PAY DATE    27.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    96.375    SPREAD	=</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ   *ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (M) 5-50	SALE LIMITS US/GB/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.375     SELL CONC  1.625     PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> NOTES     *CALL AT PAR AFTER THREE YEARS AFTER WHICH NOTES PAY</p>
<p>		19.50 PCT LESS TWO TIMES 6M LIBOR.</p>
<p>	    **ADD-ON TO OUTSTANDING 225 BLN LIRE.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
